1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,904
Every day I open a Steam demo and read its file list.
This one has three.

2
00:00:05,154 --> 00:00:07,315
And one of them is the whole game.

3
00:00:09,565 --> 00:00:15,828
It's INKBORN. You wake inside a comic nobody finished,
and an eraser is eating the page.

4
00:00:16,078 --> 00:00:21,505
You carry a sketchbook. Trace an axe,
and you're holding an axe. Ink is the cost.

5
00:00:21,755 --> 00:00:26,189
The whole demo is a hundred and fifty-one megabytes.
Three files.

6
00:00:26,439 --> 00:00:32,963
libgodotsteam. It's Godot.
After fifteen teardowns of Unity and Unreal, that's the first one.

7
00:00:33,213 --> 00:00:39,371
Godot packs everything inside the executable.
No data folder, no bundles, nothing to read.

8
00:00:39,771 --> 00:00:43,892
Every demo I open,
I read the file list first. When there is one.
